---
description: uv Dependency Management Best Practices
globs:
  - "**/pyproject.toml"
  - "**/uv.lock"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use uv as the package and project manager (replaces poetry, pip, pip-tools, virtualenv).
- Use `uv sync` to install dependencies from uv.lock.
- Use `uv add <package>` to add new dependencies.
- Use `uv add --dev <package>` to add dev dependencies.
- Use `uv run <command>` to run commands in the project environment.
- Use `uv lock` to update the lockfile after changing dependencies.
- Use `uv build` to build the package for distribution.
- Use PEP 621 standard `[project]` table in pyproject.toml (not `[tool.poetry]`).
- Prefer `[dependency-groups]` for dev dependencies over extras.